Design A — the rule lives in whoever calls `cast`:
  VoterId(1) accepted     (checked endpoint)
  VoterId(2) accepted     (checked endpoint)
  VoterId(1) accepted     (resubmit endpoint)
  VoterId(3) refused      (not signed up)
  -> 3 ballots in the box from 2 eligible voters, 19 points cast
  -> design A: MORE BALLOTS THAN VOTERS

Design B — the right to vote is a value, and casting spends it:
  VoterId(1) signed in
      ballot accepted, receipt serial 1
  VoterId(2) signed in
      ballot accepted, receipt serial 2
  VoterId(3) refused at sign-in
  VoterId(1) refused at sign-in
  VoterId(1) signed in
      ballot accepted, receipt serial 3
  -> 3 ballots in the box from 2 eligible voters, 21 points cast
  -> design B: MORE BALLOTS THAN VOTERS

Both boxes hold three ballots. Design A can be fixed at every call
site that forgot a check; design B has exactly one function to fix.
